; One complete program per step of doc/making-a-game.mld: stepNN_<slug>.ml is
; the whole game as the guide leaves it at step NN. The guide quotes only what
; each step adds, so these are the drift-guard: they compile with the default
; build, and the moment the engine moves under them `dune build` says so.
; step01_room.ml is also the program README.md quotes, and step23_controls.ml
; its rebinding snippet. The font and the pictures some steps read (step13
; onwards, step26) come from assets/, which `dune build` copies beside them in
; _build — run it once before `dune exec`.
;
; All three libraries, not just camlcast: implicit_transitive_deps is off
; repo-wide, so a stanza names what its modules' interfaces reach. A game in
; its own repository writes (libraries camlcast) and nothing else — the flag
; is this repository's discipline, not the engine's demand.
;
; Attached to no package, so nothing installs them and the -p builds opam runs
; never see them.

(executables
 (names
  step01_room
  step02_masonry
  step03_pillars
  step04_air
  step05_dressing
  step06_antechamber
  step07_component
  step08_state
  step09_gaze
  step10_burning
  step11_wisp
  step12_hud
  step13_words
  step14_prompt
  step15_gate
  step16_winch
  step17_crossings
  step18_effect
  step19_embers
  step20_store
  step21_context
  step22_check
  step23_controls
  step24_escape
  step25_launcher
  step26_shipping)
 (libraries camlcast_core camlcast camlcast_loom))
